[center][size=6][b]FMTweak Form[/b][/size]
[size=3]A mod manager for The Witcher 3 with Nexus updates, Script Merger and health checks built in[/size][/center]

[size=4][b]What it is[/b][/size]
FMTweak Form is an unofficial fork of [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/witcher3/mods/2678]The Witcher 3 Mod Manager[/url] by stefan3372 and Systemcluster. It keeps everything the original does and adds Nexus Mods updates and downloads, plus tools that used to need several separate programs.

It is made for and tested on [b]Witcher 3 Remastered[/b] (Steam and GOG, Windows 10/11). Original and Next-Gen installs are supported by the manager it builds on, but the new features have only been tested on Remastered.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[b]Nexus Mods[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Check for Updates[/b] marks every mod with a newer file on Nexus. [b]Update[/b] installs it in place of the old version and keeps its priority, enabled state and separator. The old version is backed up first and can be restored.
[*]Changelogs in the updates window, following each mod's file update chain
[*]Browse and search Witcher 3 mods on Nexus, pick a file and install it
[*]Thumbnails, categories and summaries for linked mods
[*]Requirements check: mods, expansions and tools your mods' pages say they need
[*]Finds mods not updated since Remastered, and newer versions that were
[*]Endorse from the mod list, download history, optional nxm:// link handler (links for other games are passed on to your previous manager)
[/list]

[b]Script Merger[/b]
[list]
[*]Launch Script Merger from the manager; remaining conflicts are reported when it closes
[*]Conflict warnings and a prompt to merge after installing or updating
[*]Updates Script Merger from Nexus, keeping your merges and settings
[/list]

[b]Mod list and load order[/b]
[list]
[*]Separators to group mods, drag-and-drop load order, tick several mods and toggle them at once
[*]Priorities always follow mods.settings, including edits made outside the manager
[*]Mods the game installed from mod.io are shown (display only)
[*]Import installed mods and their Nexus IDs from Relapse's Mod Manager Redux
[/list]

[b]Health and safety[/b]
[list]
[*]Health check: missing files, mods installed twice, unmerged conflicts, Sharedutils load order on Remastered (one-click fix), ReShade problems
[*]File conflicts: which mod wins when several pack the same file
[*]Backs up your newest saves before updating mods
[*]Installs and tracks files for the game's bin folder (such as ReShade add-ons) and never overwrites files it didn't install
[*]ReShade: shows the version and build, turns it on or off, updates it
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installing[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Download the main file and unzip it.
[*]Run [b]W3MM-casualfork-<version>-setup.exe[/b]. It installs for your Windows account only, without an admin prompt. Python isn't needed.
[*]On first start, the setup page finds the game through Steam or GOG and asks for Script Merger, the download folder and your Nexus API key.
[/list]
The manager checks for its own updates once a day (Help > Update Manager..., can be turned off). The installer's SHA-256 is in the README inside the zip and in the GitHub release notes.

[b]Coming from the original Witcher 3 Mod Manager?[/b] FMTweak Form uses the same settings folder, so your mod list is picked up. Back up [i]AppData\Local\The Witcher 3 Mod Manager[/i] first, and don't run both at the same time.

[size=4][b]Nexus account[/b][/size]
The Nexus features need your personal Nexus API key, from the bottom of the [url=https://next.nexusmods.com/settings/api-keys]API keys page[/url], entered under Settings > Setup... The key is stored encrypted with Windows and is only ever sent to Nexus.
[list]
[*][b]Premium:[/b] one-click updates and downloads straight from the manager.
[*][b]Free:[/b] update checks, changelogs and everything else work the same. Downloads open the Nexus page; click "Mod Manager Download" there and the manager installs the file (turn on the nxm link handler first).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Antivirus warnings[/b][/size]
The manager is a Python program packed with cx_Freeze, which some antivirus programs flag by mistake. The full source is on GitHub, and every release lists the installer's SHA-256 so you can check your download.

[size=4][b]Not supported[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Script Merger merging itself (the manager runs Script Merger; it doesn't replace it)
[*]Merging individual ini keys (ini files in bin/config/base are copied whole)
[*]The new features haven't been tried on Linux or macOS
[/list]

[size=4][b]Credits and licence[/b][/size]
Original manager by [b]stefan3372[/b], continued by [b]Systemcluster[/b] ([url=https://github.com/Systemcluster/The-Witcher-3-Mod-manager]GitHub[/url]). FMTweak Form is not made or supported by them, so please report problems here or on [url=https://github.com/mooonski/W3MM-casualfork/issues]this fork's GitHub issues[/url], not upstream.
